  "id": "negative-induction",
  "term": "negative induction",
  "definition": "Negative induction is a historical logical method described in Nyāya reasoning for testing a general rule by using a contrasting or dissimilar case. In the example given, it supports a conclusion by showing that the subject does not belong with things that have the opposite property.",
