      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s description of the example (“supports a conclusion by showing that the subject does not belong with things that have the opposite property”) is an added interpretive gloss. The packet provides the Nyāya discussion that “the ‘general rule’ or ‘universal proposition’ is to be tested by affirmative and negative induction” and then quotes arguments against the Mīmāṃsā doctrine of the eternity of sound, but it does not explicitly state the “subject does not belong with…opposite property” rationale in those terms."
